{
  // Output filename and BoardLoader data-variable name:
  //   boardName "RP2040" -> designer/boards/RP2040/RP2040.json -> const RP2040Data = {...}
  "boardName": "RP2040",

  // Fallback human-readable name shown in the designer UI.  Overridden
  // by the matching `<id>.name=` entry in a sibling-or-ancestor
  // boards.txt when one is present (matched via `<id>.build.variant=`
  // against this variant's directory name) — confirmed here via
  // ../../boards.txt: "adafruit_feather_adalogger.name=Adafruit Feather
  // RP2040 Adalogger".
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)",

  // Same parser dialect as every other RP2040 board — see
  // ../board.json for the full rationale.
  "family": "rp2040",

  // GPIO7 (BOOT button, see chipGpios below) is a genuine bidirectional
  // GPIO merely wired to a switch to GND with the RP2040's internal
  // pull-up enabled by software — not a dedicated/capacitive-only pin —
  // so it is handled entirely via the chipGpios "button" tag (full
  // capability set retained), not via inputOnlyGpios.
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],

  // Default transports — Serial only.
  "connections": ["serial"],

  "pinNotes": {},

  // pfodWeb NOTE (RP2040/RP2350 family button/LED/NeoPixel + dedicated-
  // hardware pin-exclusion audit, 2026-07-13):
  //
  // Board: Adafruit "Feather RP2040 Adalogger" (product 5743) — a
  // Feather RP2040 with an onboard microSD card slot (SPI1) for data
  // logging, a plain red status LED (D13), a single onboard status
  // NeoPixel (GPIO17), and a BOOT button also usable as a general input
  // (GPIO7). This board's own pins_arduino.h already declares a bespoke
  // (not ../generic_full/common.h) pin set correctly excluding the
  // SD-card GPIOs from its D<n> alias list, but had no board.json
  // override before this audit, so every aliased GPIO (including the
  // card-detect/CLK/MOSI/MISO/DAT1/DAT2/CS SD-card lines) defaulted to
  // full digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output capability.
  //
  // Sources consulted:
  // 1. learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-feather-rp2040-adalogger/pinouts
  //    (official Adafruit guide) — quotes verbatim:
  //      "Above the USB C connector is the D13 LED. This little red LED
  //      is controllable in CircuitPython code using board.LED, and in
  //      Arduino as PIN_LED." (GPIO13)
  //      "Above the silkscreen label for pin 24 is the status NeoPixel
  //      LED. It is connected to GPIO17."
  //      "The Boot button is the button on the right, located on GPIO7."
  //      "SCK/GPIO14 - The main SPI1 SCK," "MO/GPIO15 - The main SPI1
  //      MOSI," "MI/GPIO8 - The main SPI1 MISO" — confirms these three
  //      (this board's own PIN_SPI0_MISO/MOSI/SCK, arduino-pico's "SPI0"
  //      routed to RP2040 hardware spi1) are the genuine, header-broken-
  //      out general-purpose SPI pins.
  //      "There is no dedicated CS pin on the main SPI header itself;
  //      CS options are available on other pins (A3, D25, D13, D9 per
  //      SPI1 CS listings)" — CONFIRMS GPIO13 is merely one of several
  //      arbitrary software-selectable SS choices offered by the RP2040's
  //      GPIO mux, not real dedicated wiring, matching the
  //      adafruit_feather_scorpio false-positive precedent exactly. This
  //      board's arduino-pico-supplied pins_arduino.h had picked that
  //      same default (PIN_SPI0_SS=13u), directly colliding with the
  //      confirmed LED pin.
  //      "SD_SCK/GPIO18," "SD_MOSI/GPIO19," "SD_MISO/GPIO20,"
  //      "SD_CS/GPIO23," "SD_CARD_DETECT/GPIO16" — matches this board's
  //      own PIN_SD_CLK/CMD_MOSI/DAT0_MISO/DAT3_CS/CARD_DETECT aliases
  //      exactly, confirming all of GPIO16/18-23 are dedicated to the
  //      onboard microSD slot.
  //      "This connector uses the SCL and SDA pins for I2C, which end up
  //      being the RP2040's I2C1 peripheral" with SCL/GPIO3, SDA/GPIO2 —
  //      the STEMMA QT connector, ordinary general-purpose I2C pins, no
  //      override needed (matches this repo's other Feather STEMMA QT
  //      precedents).
  // 2. raw.githubusercontent.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr (main)
  //    boards/adafruit/feather_adalogger_rp2040/
  //    adafruit_feather_adalogger_rp2040.dts — official upstream Zephyr
  //    board port. Quotes:
  //      red_led: red_led { gpios = <&gpio0 13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; label = "Red LED"; };
  //      user_button: button { gpios = <&gpio0 7 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW | GPIO_PULL_UP)>; ... };
  //      ws2812: ws2812 { gpios = <&gpio0 17 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; chain-length = <1>; ... };
  //    This independently CONFIRMS: D13 LED is active-high; BOOT/GPIO7
  //    button is active-low with the RP2040's internal pull-up enabled;
  //    the onboard NeoPixel is GPIO17, active-high data line, single
  //    pixel (chain-length 1, not a chain).
  // 3. raw.githubusercontent.com/adafruit/circuitpython (main)
  //    ports/raspberrypi/boards/adafruit_feather_rp2040_adalogger/
  //    mpconfigboard.h — `MICROPY_HW_NEOPIXEL` on GPIO17; SD card SPI1
  //    block confirms SCK=GPIO18, MOSI=GPIO19, MISO=GPIO20, CS=GPIO23,
  //    card detect=GPIO16, default state card-inserted=true — matches
  //    every SD-card GPIO above exactly, and no MICROPY_HW_LED/APA102
  //    define beyond the plain GPIO13 LED already confirmed by source #2.
  //
  // BUG FIX (this session): pins_arduino.h originally also defined
  // `PIN_SPI0_SS (13u)` and a matching `static const uint8_t SS =
  // PIN_SPI0_SS;` line, directly colliding with the confirmed PIN_LED
  // (GPIO13) role above (see source #1's "no dedicated CS pin" quote).
  // Removed both lines (see that file's own pfodWeb NOTE) to stop
  // build_boards.js's unconditional SS-alias bus-role auto-append from
  // contaminating the GPIO13 chipGpios entry below with a spurious
  // spi_ss capability — the same bug class already fixed this session on
  // adafruit_feather_scorpio. SPI1 (the SD card's own bus, using
  // PIN_SPI1_SS/PIN_SD_DAT3_CS = GPIO23) is untouched and unaffected.
  //
  // Full findings/sources trail:
  // boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040/adafruit_feather_adalogger/notes.txt
  "chipGpios": {
    "7":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output", "button"], "note": "PIN_BUTTON/BOOT — bootloader-select pushbutton, active-low" },
    "13": { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED — onboard status LED (D13), active-high" },
    "16": { "capabilities": ["digital_input"], "note": "PIN_CARD_DETECT — onboard microSD card connector's card-detect" },
    "17": { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "led_neopixel"], "note": "PIN_NEOPIXEL — onboard single status NeoPixel (WS2812)" },
    "18": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SD_CLK / PIN_SPI1_SCK — onboard microSD card clock line" },
    "19": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SD_CMD_MOSI / PIN_SPI1_MOSI — onboard microSD CMD line" },
    "20": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SD_DAT0_MISO / PIN_SPI1_MISO — onboard microSD DAT0 line" },
    "21": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SD_DAT1 — onboard microSD card connector's DAT1 line" },
    "22": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SD_DAT2 — onboard microSD card connector's DAT2 line" },
    "23": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SD_DAT3_CS / PIN_SPI1_SS — onboard microSD chip-select" }
  },

  // Same 8-bit analogWrite() default as every other RP2040/RP2350 board.
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },

  // No hardware DAC on RP2040/RP2350.
  "dac": {},

  // RP2040's one 12-bit ADC (0-4095), ~3.3V reference — same as every
  // other RP2040 board. This board's pins_arduino.h declares no analog
  // aliases of its own (falls through to the chip-level 26-29/A0-A3
  // defaults), and this audit found no reason to override that.
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
